<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area rose slightly in the week ending March 27, an industry source said. The following are estimates, with week-ago and year-ago levels.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>		27/03/97		20/03/97		29/03/96</p>
<p> Gasoline	  550		 550-575		 600-625</p>
<p> Naphtha	   125		     100			75</p>
<p> Gas oil	 1,725	   1,700-1,750	   1,800-1,850</p>
<p> Fuel oil	  350		 325-350		     350</p>
<p> Jet		  15			15		   10-20</p>
<p>Gasoline was fairly active with a good degree of incoming material being offset by outgoing barges into Germany and cargoes going into NWE. Naphtha was quieter with incoming barrels outweighing the moderate movement into Germany to cover petchem demand.</p>
<p>Fuel saw limited business with some bunkering demand failing to draw stocks much. A small amount of jet went into the aviaiton sector.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
